<section #l1-article | `<article>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `document-containers` · Layer 1 `<article>` · JATS `<article>` · `content` `structured`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` | Document-level note render mode (#33): "bottom" (default) keeps numbered notes at the foot of the document; "margin" projects each note into a margin column beside its marker (Tufte sidenotes). Where notes COLLECT (per-note end/foot/side; per-section or per-chapter) is the per-note `placement` kwarg plus `note-scope`, not this attribute — see <note>. |

Produced by: canonical `<article>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-article-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.

<section | Conclusion>
The paper concludes here.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=article&gt; at the top with no &lt;article&gt; wrapper. The structural plugin generates the &lt;article&gt; container and the three region wrappers. &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; is promoted to &lt;article-title&gt;; &lt;meta&gt; itself survives inside &lt;article-front&gt;.*

<code #code:l1-article-2>
<article | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
<meta>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

*Explicit-form escape hatch: &lt;article | Title&gt;. The structural plugin respects the explicit wrapper. Pipe content from &lt;article&gt; becomes &lt;article-title&gt;, placed as the first child of &lt;meta&gt; (creating &lt;meta&gt; if absent, or appending if present).*

<code #code:l1-article-3>
<section | Introduction>
The introduction.

<section | Conclusion>
The conclusion.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

*No &lt;meta&gt; and no &lt;article&gt; declared. The structural plugin assumes article-shaped (the default) and wraps the sections in an implicit article. &lt;article-front&gt; is omitted because there's no metadata.*

</section>

<section #l1-book | `<book>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `document-containers` · Layer 1 `<book>` · JATS `<book>` · `content` `structured`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` | Document-level note render mode (#33): "bottom" (default) / "margin" (Tufte sidenotes). Where notes COLLECT — including per-chapter — is the per-note `placement` kwarg plus `note-scope` (a book defaults to `note-scope=chapter`), not this attribute. See <note>. |

Produced by: canonical `<book>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-book-1>
<meta type=book>
  <title | A Natural History of Elephants>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<chapter | Origins>
<section | Early ancestors>
Content here.

<chapter | Modern populations>
<section | African elephants>
Content here.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=book&gt; at the top with no &lt;book&gt; wrapper. The structural plugin generates &lt;book&gt; + the three region wrappers. Each book-part contains its own &lt;meta&gt; with the promoted &lt;book-part-title&gt;; no &lt;book-part-meta&gt; wrapper.*

<code #code:l1-book-2>
<meta type=book>
  <title | The Comprehensive Guide>
  <author | Author Name>
</meta>

<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Principles>
Content.

<chapter | Background>
Content.

<part | Part II: Applications>
<chapter | Practical Examples>
Content.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

</section>

<section #l1-book-part | `<book-part>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `document-containers` · Layer 1 `<book-part>` · JATS `<book-part>` · `content` `structured`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `chapter` `part` `appendix` `preface` `foreword` `introduction` `conclusion` `glossary` `dedication` `afterword` `colophon` `other` | The kind of book-part. Authored as `type` (the prefix is redundant inside a <book-part>); renders to the HTML/BITS attribute `book-part-type` (maps_to). Distinct from <meta type>, which is the document class. Always present in Layer 1; the shorthand layer typically supplies it via a shorthand element name (e.g., <chapter> sets it to "chapter"). |
| `numbering-style` | kwarg | `arabic` `roman` `alpha` `none` |  |
| `note-position` | kwarg | `bottom` `margin` | Document-level note render mode (#33): "bottom" / "margin". Collection (the per-note `placement` kwarg and `note-scope`) is a separate axis — see <note>. |
| `+unlisted` | boolean | default `false` | Keep this book-part out of the generated table of contents, regardless of toc-depth (#218) — e.g. a preface or an index chapter that should not appear in the contents. Display-only: it still renders; it is only absent from the contents listing. See notes/specs/toc-and-numbering.md. Authored as +unlisted; renders to the HTML attribute unlisted. |
| `+unnumbered` | boolean | default `false` | Skip this book-part's number, regardless of number-depth (#218) — e.g. an unnumbered "Introduction" chapter. Outside the numbered sequence: no number, no counter advance (the next numbered chapter continues unbroken), subtree unnumbered. (Front-matter and non-appendix back-matter are already unnumbered by region.) See notes/specs/toc-and-numbering.md. Authored as +unnumbered. |

Produced by: canonical `<book-part>` · alias `<chapter>` · alias `<part>` · alias `<appendix>` · alias `<preface>` · alias `<foreword>` · alias `<introduction>` · alias `<conclusion>` · alias `<glossary>` · alias `<dedication>` · alias `<afterword>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-book-part-1>
<chapter | Origins>
Content of the chapter.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

<code #code:l1-book-part-2>
<part | Part I: Foundations>
<chapter | First Chapter>
Content.

<chapter | Second Chapter>
Content.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

<code #code:l1-book-part-3>
<preface | A Note from the Author>
I wrote this book because...

<chapter | Chapter One>
Body content.

<appendix | Notation>
Notation conventions used in this book.
</code>

*Renders as a whole document — shown as source; see the Showcase chapter for a live multi-construct example.*

*The structural plugin places the preface in book-front, the chapter in book-body, and the appendix in book-back based on book-part-type.*

</section>

